# Platform Restoration & Modernization — Walkthrough

## Summary
The **Pharma Translation Platform** has been successfully stabilized by unifying the high-performance editing capabilities of the `v.6` backup with the modern security and administrative features of the current version. All regressions have been resolved, and the system is now fully operational and type-safe.

## Key Changes

### 1. Core Editor Engine Restoration
- **Dual-Block LangCell**: Restored the V1/Proposed editing mode with drag-and-drop block swapping.
- **Sayqallash Engine**: Fully restored the expert pharmaceutical grammar correction with red/green inline annotations and bulk-acceptance functionality.
- **AI-Powered Row Manipulation**: Re-implemented "Magic Split" and manual row reordering using `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`.
- **Rich Content Support**: Re-enabled support for inline images (`§IMG:...§`), tables (`§TBL:...§`), and mathematical formulas.

### 2. Infrastructure & Startup Stabilization
- **start_app.bat**: Fixed to correctly use the root-level virtual environment (`.venv`). Added dependency checks for `node_modules` and the Python interpreter.
- **Model Standard**: Standardized all AI endpoints to use the user-verified `claude-sonnet-4-20250514` model name.
- **API Security**: Integrated `useAuth()` to ensure all frontend-to-backend calls include the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.

### 3. User Experience & Admin Integration
- **Admin Panel Access**: Added a secure "🛡️ Admin Panel" link to the main Dashboard, visible only to users with the `admin` role.
- **Project History**: Restored the history panel with Text ID and Specialist Name tracking.
- **Type Safety**: Refactored the codebase to replace `any` types with the `RowData` interface, ensuring long-term maintainability.

